---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Grove, an open project for visual tree-based machine learning education."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Grove</p>
    <h1>Built to make trees inspectable.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Grove is an open educational project about tree-based machine learning. It
      connects plain-English explanations to from-scratch algorithms and visual
      evidence.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="lesson-body">
    <h2>Why this project exists</h2>
    <p>
      Decision trees are often introduced as diagrams and then used through a
      library. The interesting part between those moments—the search, trade-offs,
      and failure modes—deserves to be visible.
    </p>
    <p>
      The first language is English. Content and navigation are kept separate
      enough to support additional translations as the project matures.
    </p>
    <h2>Open by default</h2>
    <p>
      The implementation, training traces, visual components, and lessons are
      designed to live together in a public repository. Known simplifications
      will be documented instead of hidden.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

